#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Leaves the production-built Electron app open for human review.
 *
 * Build and launch from the repository root:
 *
 *     pnpm run review:desktop -- --sandbox <root> [--surface <name>]
 *
 * The root command rebuilds first. This launcher then reuses the same isolated
 * sandbox an agent populated for screenshot/drive/mock-mod work, detaches the
 * Electron process, and exits; closing the app window is the normal way to stop
 * it. With no --sandbox it creates a fresh one and prints its path. `--real` is
 * the explicit opt-in to the developer's actual userData and game folder.
 *
 * The window is shown without activation: it appears in the task switcher but
 * does not take keyboard focus from the developer. Its title includes the
 * worktree directory so simultaneous handoffs remain distinguishable.
 * Renderer/main output is appended to <sandbox>/review-app.log (or a temp log
 * for --real) because the detached process has no owning terminal.
 *
 * This launches `out/` directly: production renderer bundle, app:// loading and
 * production CSP, but not an electron-builder installer or release payload.
 */
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process'
import { closeSync, existsSync, openSync } from 'node:fs'
import os from 'node:os'
import path from 'node:path'
import { createRequire } from 'node:module'
